gocontroll-hmi-demo (1.0.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop gocontroll-hmi-display-recover. The HMI1 kernel (GOcontroll/linux
    gocontroll-6.12.87 at 76d8f6835f3d or later) now waits out a busy i2c-3
    when it probes the MAX25014 and the PCF85063, and reprograms the backlight
    chip itself after a power-on reset while the system keeps running. The
    userspace helper was a workaround for exactly those cases. preinst stops
    the old service on upgrade and purges its enable state, so no dangling
    sysinit.target.wants link is left behind. Requires the new kernel; stay on
    1.0.4 with an older one.
  * Drop the i2c-tools dependency and the gpiod recommendation; only the
    helper used them.
  * Wait up to 15 s for /dev/dri/card1 in both the splash and the dashboard.
    The helper used to gate the splash on it; without that, and with the
    kernel now taking up to ~10 s to bring the display chain up on a busy bus,
    opening the device once and giving up left a black screen.
  * Fade the backlight in on its own perceptual ramp (1.2 s, gamma 2.2)
    instead of the logo's ease-out. Tied to the logo it reached 39 of 50 in
    about 0.3 s, which looked like a hard switch-on.
  * Do not start the splash from postinst. It only makes sense at boot; on an
    install or upgrade the dashboard holds DRM master, so the splash failed
    at once and left a failed unit behind. It stays enabled for the next boot.

 -- GOcontroll <info@gocontroll.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0100

gocontroll-hmi-demo (1.0.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fade the backlight in with the splash logo. The HMI1 kernel now leaves
    the MAX25014 at brightness 0 until userspace has a picture to show, so
    the panel no longer lights up on an empty frame at boot. The splash
    raises it alongside the logo's own fade, to 50% of max_brightness or
    GOCONTROLL_SPLASH_BRIGHTNESS (percent), and leaves it alone when
    something earlier in the boot already turned it on.

 -- GOcontroll <info@gocontroll.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0100

gocontroll-hmi-demo (1.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Declare the font licences. The binary embeds glyph bitmaps rendered from
    Montserrat (SIL OFL 1.1) and, in lv_font_montserrat_14_ext.c, from Font
    Awesome Free 5 (CC BY 4.0 icons, OFL 1.1 fonts). debian/copyright declared
    the whole package Expat and named neither, while both licences require the
    notice to travel with the distribution. Add stanzas for them, ship the
    verbatim texts in /usr/share/doc/gocontroll-hmi-demo/licenses/, and put an
    attribution header on the generated font file — lv_font_conv does not emit
    one, so it has to be maintained by hand across regenerations.
  * Stop declaring thirdparty/lvgl/* as Expat wholesale. LVGL itself is, but
    the upstream tree bundles frogfs (MPL-2.0), vg_lite_driver (proprietary
    Vivante), gif (Apache-2.0), lodepng and nanovg (Zlib), lz4/TLSF/barcode
    (BSD) and tjpgd. None are compiled into this package, which is now stated
    explicitly rather than papered over.
  * Give gocontroll_demo and assets/ their own stanzas: the Simulink binary was
    silently covered by Files: *, and the Expat licence over the logos conveys
    no trademark rights, which is now spelled out.

 -- GOcontroll <info@gocontroll.com>  Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:05:00 +0200

gocontroll-hmi-demo (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read the serial number from where it actually lives. identify.c read
    /etc/go-sn, a file that does not exist on any image — the Information
    screen has always shown "-" for Serial. go-sn stores the 19-byte string at
    the start of the GPT partition labelled 'serial', falling back to the last
    sector of /dev/mmcblk0 on legacy units; read both in that order, validate
    the four-group layout, and keep the field empty when nothing is programmed.
  * Show the demo's own version on the Information screen, under System.
    CMakeLists.txt parses it out of the top of this changelog and passes it in
    as GOCONTROLL_HMI_DEMO_VERSION, so the version on screen cannot drift from
    the version of the .deb.
  * Build-Depend on libevdev-dev. CMakeLists.txt has always required it through
    pkg_check_modules, but it was missing from the list, so the build failed at
    configure time on any machine that did not happen to have it installed.

 -- GOcontroll <info@gocontroll.com>  Tue, 11 Aug 2026 15:10:00 +0200

gocontroll-hmi-demo (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop two boot orderings that were never real preconditions. Measured on a
    Moduline HMI1 with systemd-analyze critical-chain, kernel time 1.12s in
    both runs:
    - splash: no longer ordered after systemd-tmpfiles-setup and
      local-fs.target. The asset sits on the root fs and card1 comes from
      devtmpfs, so both only added latency: 3.37s -> 2.68s.
    - demo: no longer ordered after systemd-user-sessions, which pulls in
      network.target and NetworkManager. The Simulink backend, the actual
      precondition, was ready at 1.7s: 5.54s -> 4.48s.
  * Only install signals.json and parameters.json when they are present. Both
    are generated per Simulink build from the .a2l, are gitignored and have
    never been committed, so the unconditional install made dpkg-buildpackage
    fail on every fresh clone. When they are absent src/config.c already falls
    back to addresses derived from the ELF symbols of the bundled
    gocontroll_demo binary.

 -- GOcontroll <info@gocontroll.com>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 14:42:35 +0200

